data.content:
Since `TimestampFormatter` is a `static` class, it can't participate in DI directly (no constructor injection). You have two good options:

### Option 1 — Make it a non-static class (recommended)
Convert to an instance class, inject `TimeProvider`, and register it in DI:

```csharp
public class TimestampFormatter(TimeProvider timeProvider)
{
    public string Now() => timeProvider.GetUtcNow().ToString("O");
}
```

### Option 2 — Keep it static, pass `TimeProvider` as a parameter
```csharp
public static class TimestampFormatter
{
    public static string Now(TimeProvider timeProvider)
        => timeProvider.GetUtcNow().ToString("O");
}
```

**Option 1 is the better path** since `TimeProvider` is already in your DI container — callers just inject `TimestampFormatter` instead of calling a static method. It's also straightforward to test (pass `FakeTimeProvider`).

